# Sub-repositories ensured by `make core.repos` (runs as part of `make install`).
# Copy this file to the project root as `subrepos.conf` and fill in your remotes.
#
# One entry per line, format: <folder>=<git-remote>
# Blank lines and lines starting with '#' are ignored.
#
# A missing folder is cloned, an existing one only gets its `origin` corrected —
# the working tree and the checked-out branch are never touched, so the target is
# safe to re-run. Set XO_SUBREPOS_BRANCH in .env.local to clone a branch other
# than the remote default.
#
# When a repository moves, change the remote here and re-run `make core.repos`;
# existing clones are repointed in place.
#
# This replaces git submodules: no .gitmodules, and the folders stay plain clones.

# api=git@github.com:your-org/your-api.git
# frontend=git@github.com:your-org/your-frontend.git
#
# An entry for "./" keeps the origin of the project repository itself in sync:
# ./=git@github.com:your-org/your-project.git
